grund integrations — print or install the clickable-citation terminal/editor integrations.

Usage:  grund integrations [<client>] [--write] [--conversation plain|link] [--format text|json]

With no client, detects the terminal/editor from the environment and prints
what applies. With a client — kitty, tmux, vscode, or wezterm — prints that
integration's snippet and the grund-open resolver; --write installs it as a
managed, idempotent block instead of printing. A write also records the local
conversation preference and updates global agent instructions; override the
plain default with --conversation link. --format json emits a plan.

Preview and install examples:
  grund integrations                    # detect and list what applies
  grund integrations wezterm            # print the snippet + resolver
  grund integrations wezterm --write    # install it, idempotently
  grund integrations wezterm --write --conversation link

Exit:  0 printed or installed · 2 invalid options, missing client, or a newer block.
